WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.529
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:07.799 --> 00:11.169
The officers are having a sports day. Why are we the ones suffering?

3
00:11.169 --> 00:13.749
You're saying they can't score because of this tiny rock?

4
00:13.749 --> 00:16.609
Then they shouldn't be playing in the "Military-sliga."

5
00:17.409 --> 00:21.789
I'd rather have a cushy job working on the nets like them.

6
00:21.789 --> 00:25.389
- Is that based on rank or volunteering? - They were actually handpicked.

7
00:25.389 --> 00:28.049
What, are they former soccer players?

8
00:28.049 --> 00:30.729
What was it? Oh, a fisheries college?

9
00:30.729 --> 00:34.149
But what does a fisheries college have to do with soccer nets?

10
00:34.149 --> 00:37.409
Nets are nets! Fisheries college, nets!

11
00:37.409 --> 00:41.855
They picked him because they thought he'd be good with nets.

12
00:41.855 --> 00:44.429
Hey, you idiot. Are those nets the same as these?

13
00:44.429 --> 00:45.949
- To the right. - Yes, sir.

14
00:45.949 --> 00:48.189
Then is that guy a ball boy because he's an engineering major?

15
00:48.189 --> 00:50.039
I'm sorry.

16
00:50.039 --> 00:52.949
- Oh, you're right. - What?

17
00:52.949 --> 00:55.969
- He's an aerospace engineering major! - Why would they use a genius for that?

18
00:55.969 --> 00:59.810
Why else? This is the military.

19
00:59.810 --> 01:04.217
They said his trajectory calculations are so sharp,

20
01:04.217 --> 01:06.349
they picked him to grab the ball before it lands.

21
01:06.349 --> 01:10.769
Man, that's insane. What about that guy? An art major?

22
01:10.769 --> 01:14.169
He's a fashion design major.

23
01:14.169 --> 01:16.649
They picked him because they thought he'd be good at drawing lines.

24
01:16.649 --> 01:19.189
Now that you mention it, those lines are a work of art.

25
01:19.189 --> 01:22.791
The way they assigned specialties at the training center was ridiculous.

26
01:22.791 --> 01:25.809
Still, I'm jealous you have a major.

27
01:25.809 --> 01:29.729
- Come on, you can be a freshman soon. - I will, you punk.

28
01:29.729 --> 01:32.649
But what are you going to major in?

29
01:32.649 --> 01:34.739
International Trade.

30
01:35.389 --> 01:38.424
International Trade? Are you going to travel the whole world?

31
01:38.424 --> 01:40.509
I'm going to take Jeon Se Gye with me.

32
01:40.509 --> 01:43.469
Wow, that rhyme was crazy. You're really a sergeant now.

33
01:43.469 --> 01:47.649
Right, when we were painting, the First Sergeant asked,

34
01:47.649 --> 01:51.329
"Dong Woo, you go to Hong University? Do painting work."

35
01:51.329 --> 01:54.147
"I'm a chemical engineering major."

36
01:54.147 --> 01:57.329
"Then I thought you must be good at mixing paint and thinner!"

37
01:57.329 --> 01:59.077
Chungseong! Love you, sir!

38
01:59.077 --> 02:03.189
- Right. Everyone, listen up! - Attention!

39
02:03.189 --> 02:06.919
Are any of you landscape architecture majors?

40
02:06.919 --> 02:09.669
- No, sir! - Good grief...

41
02:09.669 --> 02:11.429
Is it for mowing the lawn?

42
02:11.429 --> 02:14.249
- No. - Then why the landscape architecture major?

43
02:14.249 --> 02:17.099
To set up the camouflage nets!

44
02:17.099 --> 02:20.709
First Sergeant, what does camouflage have to do with landscape architecture?

45
02:20.709 --> 02:22.613
It's related, you punk!

46
02:23.429 --> 02:28.569
- By the way, are you all going on leave? - Yes, sir.

47
02:28.569 --> 02:33.956
That's strange. You guys aren't the type to quit smoking.

48
02:33.956 --> 02:38.269
- 3rd Squad, let's do our best today! - Let's go, let's go!

49
02:38.269 --> 02:42.309
Choi Byeong Nam, stop dancing! Focus, you punk!

50
02:42.309 --> 02:43.393
Keep up the good work.

51
02:43.393 --> 02:45.282
- Thank you. - Thank you, sir.

52
02:45.895 --> 02:48.469
Take the old ones down, put the new ones up.

53
02:48.469 --> 02:52.869
- Check the inventory thoroughly. - Yes, sir.

54
02:52.869 --> 02:54.229
Hey!

55
02:54.229 --> 02:55.269
Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

56
02:55.269 --> 02:58.389
If Jeon Sekai doesn't work and just gives orders, tell me right away.

57
02:58.389 --> 03:02.549
- No, sir! He always takes good care of me! - Oh, First Sergeant, I'm not like that.

58
03:02.549 --> 03:04.049
Let's see if you're still like that when you're a Sergeant.

59
03:04.049 --> 03:06.979
Well, I'll think about that then.

60
03:06.979 --> 03:08.769
Look at this guy. He's a real slacker now.

61
03:08.769 --> 03:11.469
Private Jeon Sekai! Thank you!

62
03:11.469 --> 03:14.111
I have to go check on the other guys, so keep up the good work.

63
03:14.111 --> 03:15.769
Yes, sir!

64
03:15.769 --> 03:18.329
Chungseong! Love you!

65
03:18.329 --> 03:23.309
The Company Commander told me to collect the "sonagis (Diary)" from the 1st Squad.

66
03:23.309 --> 03:25.009
- Hyeon Uk. - Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

67
03:25.009 --> 03:26.709
- You do it. - Yes, sir!

68
03:26.709 --> 03:29.748
- Jeon Sekai, you lead him. - Yes, sir!

69
03:31.105 --> 03:32.229
Hyeon Uk!

70
03:32.229 --> 03:33.755
Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

71
03:33.755 --> 03:35.929
- I'm going to the bathroom. - Yes, sir.

72
03:35.929 --> 03:38.569
I'll come get you when I'm done, so wait in the 1st Squad room.

73
03:38.569 --> 03:40.629
- Yes, sir! - Collect all the sonagis!

74
03:40.629 --> 03:42.089
Yes, sir!

75
03:42.089 --> 03:46.489
It'll take a while. I haven't been able to take my favorite medicine lately.

76
03:46.489 --> 03:49.019
- Have a good one, sir! - Right.

77
04:00.193 --> 04:02.773
[Sonagi - My Precious Barracks Diary]

78
04:19.379 --> 04:21.980
[Sonagi - My Precious Barracks Diary]

79
04:38.109 --> 04:41.822
I pricked my finger three times while sewing.

80
04:45.109 --> 04:46.529
Is it not working?

81
04:46.529 --> 04:48.772
I think the needle is weird.

82
04:48.772 --> 04:51.792
But my buddy, Hyeon Uk, helped me.

83
04:51.792 --> 04:54.769
Good job. Do it like this...

84
04:54.769 --> 04:57.297
I'm so glad I have a buddy.

85
04:57.297 --> 04:59.931
Oh, as expected of a buddy.

86
05:00.689 --> 05:03.049
I want ganjjajang!

87
05:03.049 --> 05:05.689
- Should I get gochu jjamppong? - Gochu jjamppong is a masterpiece.

88
05:05.689 --> 05:08.489
We shared a Choco Pie I secretly brought in the bathroom.

89
05:08.489 --> 05:10.590
Where did you get this?

90
05:12.669 --> 05:17.539
The best food in the world was Choco Pie.

91
05:19.169 --> 05:22.447
Even with the hard training, strangely, it wasn't hard at all.

92
05:22.447 --> 05:25.029
I feel like I have another memory.

93
05:25.029 --> 05:26.529
Thank you, my comrades!

94
05:26.529 --> 05:28.889
Geez, I should put this here.

95
05:28.889 --> 05:31.109
I'll put it here. Man.

96
05:31.109 --> 05:34.109
Hyeon Uk went to the hospital due to an injury.

97
05:34.109 --> 05:37.749
I hope it's not a serious injury...

98
05:37.749 --> 05:40.723
I'm worried about when he'll be back.

99
05:40.723 --> 05:42.729
Thank you for taking care of me.

100
05:42.729 --> 05:47.469
Finally, I leave tomorrow. Time really does fly.

101
05:47.469 --> 05:51.869
The sad part is leaving without even saying goodbye to Hyeon Uk.

102
05:51.869 --> 05:55.814
I'm so curious to know how he's doing.

103
05:55.814 --> 05:58.056
We promised to meet up.

104
05:58.754 --> 06:01.890
I believe we'll be able to meet again someday.

105
06:02.749 --> 06:04.893
He's doing well, right?

106
06:07.773 --> 06:10.245
- Something unbelievable happened! - Reporting! Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

107
06:10.245 --> 06:12.273
I can't believe Hyeon Uk joined our unit as a recruit!

108
06:12.273 --> 06:16.693
- I received the order! - I just found out he left because he was sick.

109
06:16.693 --> 06:18.733
I should treat him well since we met again!

110
06:18.733 --> 06:19.644
Is he a new recruit?

111
06:19.644 --> 06:21.589
Hyeon Uk and I must be meant to be.

112
06:21.589 --> 06:22.841
Remember this name.

113
06:22.841 --> 06:24.329
Hyeon Uk.

114
06:24.329 --> 06:25.793
Hyeon Uk.

115
06:25.793 --> 06:27.533
- Hyeon Uk. - Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

116
06:27.533 --> 06:30.516
Hey, just relax when it's just the two of us.

117
06:30.516 --> 06:34.453
Would it have been okay if Hyeon Uk took the ambulance instead of me?

118
06:34.453 --> 06:38.753
I should've been the one who got hurt. I'm so, so sorry.

119
06:38.753 --> 06:42.172
I want to ask for his forgiveness even now.

120
06:57.687 --> 07:00.212
[My best buddy!] [October 20, 2011]

121
07:30.033 --> 07:33.353
- Did you find everything? - Yes, I've got it all!

122
07:33.353 --> 07:35.952
- Let's go. - Yes, sir!

123
07:48.013 --> 07:51.043
- Sit down. - Yes, sir!

124
07:52.220 --> 07:53.392
[EP06. Tangled Laundry]

125
07:53.392 --> 07:55.900
This is just a formality to see if the soldiers are

126
07:55.900 --> 07:57.853
showing any signs of trouble.

127
07:57.853 --> 08:00.115
They say focus on Privates,

128
08:00.115 --> 08:02.980
but it's hard for Corporals, Sergeants, and the Battalion Commander...

129
08:02.980 --> 08:07.073
the Company Commander, Sergeant Major, First Sergeant, and even the stray cats.

130
08:07.073 --> 08:08.947
The vending machine lady has it hard,

131
08:08.947 --> 08:12.833
and the dogs out front too. Everyone in the military has it hard, right?

132
08:12.833 --> 08:14.733
No, sir.

133
08:17.853 --> 08:20.749
You and Min Seok must have been close.

134
08:21.753 --> 08:22.893
Yes, we were.

135
08:22.893 --> 08:26.002
I see. Make sure you two get even closer from now on!

136
08:26.002 --> 08:27.382
Yes, sir!

137
08:27.382 --> 08:29.693
Take it back now.

138
08:29.693 --> 08:31.403
Yes, sir.

139
08:33.733 --> 08:36.027
- Sir... - Do you have something to say?

140
08:39.686 --> 08:41.953
It's about what you told me before.

141
08:41.953 --> 08:45.713
When? I nag people so much all over the place.

142
08:45.713 --> 08:47.199
It's about what you said to me at the bathhouse.

143
08:47.199 --> 08:49.027
Ah, right.

144
08:50.893 --> 08:56.133
Even if I couldn't erase everything that happened in the civilian world,

145
08:56.133 --> 09:00.233
and even if I made a mistake here, is that still valid?

146
09:00.233 --> 09:03.018
Of course it is.

147
09:03.644 --> 09:05.323
You're one of my boys.

148
09:13.393 --> 09:14.816
Yes, sir.

149
09:16.433 --> 09:18.970
My father passed away early,

150
09:18.970 --> 09:21.244
so I had to do everything well on my own.

151
09:22.453 --> 09:25.913
Whenever that happened, I envied my friends who had fathers...

152
09:25.913 --> 09:27.407
I'm sorry.

153
09:30.413 --> 09:33.693
Whenever that happened, I envied my friends who had fathers.

154
09:33.693 --> 09:36.618
Especially those who had successful fathers.

155
09:38.031 --> 09:43.066
I think that's why my resentment was aimed at Corporal Park Min Seok.

156
09:44.233 --> 09:46.026
Back at training camp...

157
09:52.634 --> 09:55.918
So, because of the perks Min Seok got

158
09:55.918 --> 09:58.932
as the division commander's son...

159
09:58.932 --> 10:03.623
you wanted to ruin Min Seok out of spite

160
10:03.623 --> 10:06.653
because you felt you lost a year to injury.

161
10:06.653 --> 10:12.613
But now you realize it was all a misunderstanding, right?

162
10:12.613 --> 10:14.153
Yes, sir. That is correct.

163
10:14.153 --> 10:18.793
I will take full responsibility and accept any punishment without complaint.

164
10:18.793 --> 10:20.533
I am truly sorry.

165
10:20.533 --> 10:23.362
You'll accept any punishment, huh?

166
10:24.666 --> 10:26.953
Well, this was clearly intentional.

167
10:26.953 --> 10:30.103
If something serious had happened...

168
10:30.839 --> 10:33.553
And to the division commander's son, too.

169
10:33.553 --> 10:37.233
This could get quite complicated.

170
10:37.233 --> 10:41.213
It's my fault, so I'll take responsibility!

171
10:41.213 --> 10:42.719
Is that so?

172
10:42.719 --> 10:44.402
Yes, sir!

173
10:48.673 --> 10:51.913
This guy is even more something than I thought.

174
10:51.913 --> 10:53.870
I didn't expect this.

175
10:56.613 --> 10:58.363
Pardon?

176
10:58.973 --> 11:01.655
Min Seok came to see me a few days ago.

177
11:03.529 --> 11:07.960
Corporal Park Min Seok here to see the Company Commander. May I enter?

178
11:07.960 --> 11:09.660
Come in.

179
11:14.090 --> 11:17.315
Chungseong! Love you! I'm here to talk.

180
11:17.315 --> 11:18.470
Alright, have a seat.

181
11:18.470 --> 11:19.806
Yes, sir.

182
11:25.519 --> 11:27.560
So, what's on your mind?

183
11:28.182 --> 11:31.384
I have something to tell you...

184
11:31.384 --> 11:34.193
Actually, I have a favor to ask.

185
11:34.193 --> 11:36.280
A favor? What is it?

186
11:36.280 --> 11:39.553
It's about Private Kim Hyeon Uk.

187
11:39.553 --> 11:41.693
Go ahead.

188
11:41.693 --> 11:46.713
This might sound a bit strange, but from now on,

189
11:46.713 --> 11:51.273
no matter what mistake Hyeon Uk makes or what trouble he causes,

190
11:51.273 --> 11:55.053
could you please say it's all my fault and my responsibility?

191
11:55.053 --> 11:57.303
Are you predicting that he'll cause trouble?

192
11:57.303 --> 12:01.393
No, sir! It's not that...

193
12:01.393 --> 12:05.153
I did something wrong to him...

194
12:05.153 --> 12:09.145
And I'm worried he might act out because of that.

195
12:09.145 --> 12:13.152
I'll look after him so he doesn't,

196
12:13.152 --> 12:15.193
and I'll make sure nothing happens.

197
12:15.193 --> 12:20.555
Well, if you say so, Min Seok, I should trust you.

198
12:21.665 --> 12:23.500
Thank you, sir.

199
12:25.345 --> 12:28.665
- Min Seok. - Corporal Park Min Seok!

200
12:28.665 --> 12:33.011
It's tough, isn't it? Living as the division commander's son.

201
12:35.745 --> 12:37.595
No, sir...

202
12:39.176 --> 12:43.285
Hey, don't cry. I'm not really a fan of that.

203
12:43.285 --> 12:45.157
It's the first time...

204
12:45.807 --> 12:47.836
anyone's asked me if it was hard.

205
12:48.977 --> 12:54.205
Because I'm the division commander's son, everyone just says they're jealous,

206
12:54.205 --> 12:56.454
and that I'm so lucky...

207
12:57.905 --> 13:01.685
I'm sure it's been hard.

208
13:01.685 --> 13:03.991
I was afraid that if I messed up,

209
13:03.991 --> 13:07.161
[Division Commander, Park Chun Gyu] I'd bring shame to my father...

210
13:07.161 --> 13:11.836
Even as a corporal, I'm still so nervous,

211
13:12.543 --> 13:15.265
and then I make more mistakes...

212
13:15.265 --> 13:19.805
I was so afraid of people saying I got special treatment,

213
13:19.805 --> 13:23.575
that I tried my absolute hardest to do my best at everything.

214
13:24.865 --> 13:27.259
Actually, the misunderstanding with Hyeon Uk

215
13:27.259 --> 13:31.405
started because I'm the division commander's son.

216
13:31.405 --> 13:35.940
So from now on, I don't want to be Park Min Seok, the division commander's son.

217
13:35.940 --> 13:41.745
I want to clear the air as just Corporal Park Min Seok.

218
13:41.745 --> 13:44.869
But I think I'll need some time...

219
13:45.585 --> 13:48.887
If Hyeon Uk causes trouble in the meantime,

220
13:48.887 --> 13:52.365
please just say it's all my fault,

221
13:52.365 --> 13:56.605
and that I should be the one to be punished. I'd really appreciate it.

222
13:56.605 --> 14:02.425
Wow, Min Seok. You're becoming more and more like a real soldier.

223
14:02.425 --> 14:06.932
Taking responsibility for the situation and your junior

224
14:06.932 --> 14:09.985
shows you'll be a great leader.

225
14:09.985 --> 14:14.459
Actually, you're already a good senior, Min Seok.

226
14:15.365 --> 14:17.465
Do you really think so?

227
14:17.465 --> 14:22.362
Hearing you say that, Company Commander, makes me feel like it might be true.

228
14:23.420 --> 14:27.633
Right! Since we're on the subject, is there anything I can do to help?

229
14:27.633 --> 14:30.625
Oh? Could you... really help me?

230
14:30.625 --> 14:33.165
Of course. It's for one of my own men.

231
14:33.165 --> 14:37.503
Sir, have you ever seen the movie "Cyrano Agency?"

232
14:37.503 --> 14:41.785
- I have. Why? - I really love that movie.

233
14:41.785 --> 14:43.500
Just like in the movie,

234
14:43.500 --> 14:47.805
I think I need some time to talk to Hyeon Uk alone.

235
14:47.805 --> 14:49.465
Should I schedule your shifts together?

236
14:49.465 --> 14:54.286
I thought about that, but a guard shift might be a bit too short...

237
14:54.286 --> 14:56.545
You're quite picky for someone asking for a favor.

238
14:56.545 --> 14:57.785
I'm sorry, sir.

239
14:57.785 --> 15:00.983
No, it's fine. I get what you mean.

240
15:00.983 --> 15:03.027
Yes! And...

241
15:03.027 --> 15:04.425
Why are there so many?

242
15:04.425 --> 15:08.226
You can just pick a few from the list.

243
15:12.045 --> 15:15.445
So that's why all those things happened lately.

244
15:15.445 --> 15:18.625
Director Park Min Seok's "Kim Hyeon Uk Reconciliation Agency?"

245
15:18.625 --> 15:21.465
And we have some great actors, too.

246
15:21.465 --> 15:23.905
- Okay, keep up the good work. - Chungseong! Love you!

247
15:23.905 --> 15:25.505
Take care, sir.

248
15:25.505 --> 15:27.704
It'll take a while.

249
15:27.704 --> 15:30.514
I haven't been able to take my favorite medicine lately.

250
15:30.514 --> 15:33.945
- Chungseong! Love you! - Right, love you too.

251
15:33.945 --> 15:35.847
Private Jeon Se Gye!

252
15:36.979 --> 15:41.191
I think he played me. But I feel good about it.

253
15:41.191 --> 15:45.112
You coming to see me wasn't in the script, though.

254
15:45.112 --> 15:50.405
He's changed a lot... Corporal Park Min Seok.

255
15:50.405 --> 15:52.505
He's not the same Park Min Seok from before, is he?

256
15:52.505 --> 15:57.025
Min Seok went through a lot without using his father's influence at all.

257
15:57.025 --> 16:01.245
Hyeon Uk must have grown a lot through this as well.

258
16:01.245 --> 16:03.195
Company Commander.

259
16:03.195 --> 16:06.085
- Thank you. - Hey, you should be thanking Min Seok.

260
16:06.085 --> 16:10.525
Still, I'm grateful to you too, sir.

261
16:10.525 --> 16:12.005
Sure.

262
16:13.685 --> 16:17.955
But sir, about that script...

263
16:21.285 --> 16:23.055
Yes?

264
16:24.151 --> 16:26.045
- Chungseong! - Chungseong!

265
16:26.045 --> 16:28.075
Battalion Commander, you're still here?

266
16:28.075 --> 16:29.925
- Yeah. - Should I call the Company Commander?

267
16:29.925 --> 16:32.365
No, that's fine. The First Sergeant is here.

268
16:32.365 --> 16:33.445
Yes, sir.

269
16:33.445 --> 16:36.025
The guys in 2nd Company did a great job.

270
16:36.025 --> 16:38.135
I knew they'd pull it off.

271
16:38.135 --> 16:40.948
The guys were so desperate for an overnight pass

272
16:40.948 --> 16:43.214
that they were full of venom.

273
16:44.505 --> 16:46.465
Actually, this anti-smoking campaign...

274
16:46.465 --> 16:50.345
I wanted to see how united and determined our soldiers could be.

275
16:50.345 --> 16:52.305
That was my intention.

276
16:52.305 --> 16:55.312
I think they've proven themselves enough.

277
16:55.312 --> 16:59.485
- Sir? Then... - Let's end the campaign here.

278
16:59.485 --> 17:03.625
If we push it further, it might backfire.

279
17:03.625 --> 17:06.905
Yes, sir! The guys will be thrilled.

280
17:06.905 --> 17:11.945
- First Sergeant, please make the announcement. - Yes, sir. Chungseong!

281
17:11.945 --> 17:15.414
- Chungseong! Good work, sir. - Right, get some rest.

282
17:17.952 --> 17:20.105
- Hey, what are you doing? - Corporal Sung Yoon Mo.

283
17:20.105 --> 17:23.245
- Make the announcement. - Yes, sir!

284
17:23.245 --> 17:28.239
Attention. This is the admin office. As of today, the anti-smoking campaign

285
17:28.239 --> 17:29.966
has ended.

286
17:29.966 --> 17:34.334
Repeating. As of today, the anti-smoking campaign

287
17:34.334 --> 17:35.665
has ended.

288
17:35.665 --> 17:40.142
Personnel from Barracks 3 are going on group overnight leave tomorrow.

289
17:40.142 --> 17:45.523
Please submit your leave plans to the admin office before roll call. That is all.

290
17:45.523 --> 17:47.434
Company, attention!

291
17:47.434 --> 17:50.205
Salute Lieutenant Oh Seok Jin for granting us leave!

292
17:50.205 --> 17:52.644
- Chungseong! Love you! - Chungseong! Love you!

293
17:52.644 --> 17:54.635
Come on in!

294
17:56.385 --> 17:57.785
Thank you.

295
17:57.785 --> 18:00.385
So, what's the first thing you'll do once we're out?

296
18:00.385 --> 18:02.585
- Let's hit the pool hall first. - No way.

297
18:02.585 --> 18:06.325
You need sundae soup and a midday drink to wash away the military stress.

298
18:06.325 --> 18:08.922
How about karaoke after the midday drink?

299
18:08.922 --> 18:11.865
- Let's keep the energy high. - Karaoke sounds good.

300
18:11.865 --> 18:14.796
- Right? - I'm tone-deaf, so no.

301
18:15.476 --> 18:17.801
Let's just go to a PC cafe and then drink.

302
18:17.801 --> 18:19.653
But we're already having soju with soup.

303
18:19.653 --> 18:21.075
That's just a side drink.

304
18:21.075 --> 18:23.881
A real drinking session has a different vibe and snacks.

305
18:23.881 --> 18:27.148
I'm fine with anything as long as it's food.

306
18:27.148 --> 18:30.929
How about taking a group photo?

307
18:30.929 --> 18:32.281
What are we, high schoolers?

308
18:32.281 --> 18:35.081
- Hey, photos are all that remain. - Gosh, how cheesy...

309
18:35.081 --> 18:38.401
- Let's take one anyway. - I think it's a good idea too!

310
18:38.401 --> 18:39.821
If Se Gye's in, I'm in!

311
18:39.821 --> 18:41.705
- Okay. - Love you guys.

312
18:41.705 --> 18:45.379
I'll just fill in the blanks on the plan and submit it.

313
18:45.379 --> 18:46.909
[Leave Plan]

314
18:47.585 --> 18:50.141
But...

315
18:50.141 --> 18:53.501
Everyone will recognize me outside. What should I do?

316
18:53.501 --> 18:56.661
Right, this guy is Jeon Se Gye.

317
18:56.661 --> 18:58.141
Should we make him wear a mask?

318
18:58.141 --> 19:00.661
The way you look now, anyone would just see you as a soldier.

319
19:00.661 --> 19:03.648
Like, Soldier 1, 2, 3... maybe 4?

320
19:05.161 --> 19:09.525
Are you... talking about me? I've still got my star power.

321
19:09.525 --> 19:12.515
I am Jeon Se Gye.

322
19:14.612 --> 19:16.541
Where are you going? What now?

323
19:16.541 --> 19:19.520
- He's starting again. - It's time for his medicine.

324
19:21.954 --> 19:25.998
An aura that even the dampness of a poncho cannot hide.

325
19:25.998 --> 19:29.222
An unavoidable gaze, a femme fatale...

326
19:29.222 --> 19:31.293
- Ugh, the smell. - He's at it again.

327
19:31.293 --> 19:33.226
Jeon Sekai.

328
19:34.821 --> 19:36.091
Jeon Sekai.

329
19:36.091 --> 19:37.594
I just scored a point.

330
19:37.594 --> 19:39.561
I'm here to avoid the disaster.

331
19:39.561 --> 19:40.701
Oh, right. This.

332
19:40.701 --> 19:43.501
I'll go turn this in.

333
19:43.501 --> 19:45.781
Oh, I... I'll go too!

334
19:52.854 --> 19:54.511
[Weekly Diary] [Time to talk to Hyeon Uk]

335
19:56.070 --> 19:57.661
Hyeon Uk.

336
19:57.661 --> 19:58.824
Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

337
19:58.824 --> 20:01.681
- Did you polish your boots? - Yes, I did.

338
20:01.681 --> 20:03.681
- You did? - Yes, sir.

339
20:03.681 --> 20:06.841
You're very fast.

340
20:06.841 --> 20:08.341
Carry on. Keep going.

341
20:08.341 --> 20:09.876
Yes, sir.

342
20:12.254 --> 20:13.922
About that script...

343
20:13.922 --> 20:17.121
Is there anything else left in the script?

344
20:17.121 --> 20:21.441
As "Spoiler Mario," I can't just sit back and do nothing.

345
20:21.441 --> 20:25.621
I'll tell you since it's you. Come here. What's next is...

346
20:25.621 --> 20:28.230
Min Seok thought the misunderstanding was cleared

347
20:28.230 --> 20:33.481
and would look for a time to talk.

348
20:33.481 --> 20:37.091
Talking while making a suicide prevention knot during duty.

349
20:37.091 --> 20:42.221
Corporals usually do it for privates, but I saw yours wasn't done...

350
20:42.221 --> 20:43.834
What's this?

351
20:45.411 --> 20:46.745
It definitely wasn't there.

352
20:46.745 --> 20:49.067
Is something wrong?

353
20:49.067 --> 20:51.500
No, no.

354
20:51.500 --> 20:55.520
If that fails, was it talking over ramen?

355
20:55.520 --> 20:56.840
Do you want some ramen?

356
20:56.840 --> 20:58.741
Shin Ramyun is too spicy for me.

357
20:58.741 --> 21:00.961
I have all different kinds anyway.

358
21:00.961 --> 21:03.741
He said he'd prepare all kinds in case you wanted something specific.

359
21:03.741 --> 21:05.941
- Pick one! - I have all kinds too.

360
21:05.941 --> 21:08.161
Really?

361
21:08.161 --> 21:11.705
- Really? Okay, good job. - Enjoy your meal.

362
21:20.341 --> 21:23.221
Failed to talk over ramen...

363
21:23.221 --> 21:27.396
Getting locked in storage, vending machine... The laundry drying area! Okay!

364
21:33.237 --> 21:35.237
Hey, watch out!

365
21:40.175 --> 21:41.859
It's raining.

366
21:45.737 --> 21:48.898
- We should take these down quickly. - Yes, sir.

367
21:49.801 --> 21:53.021
Huh? Corporal Park Min Seok. I think the ceiling is leaking.

368
21:53.021 --> 21:54.381
You're right.

369
21:54.381 --> 21:57.601
I should tell the First Sergeant later.

370
21:57.601 --> 22:01.033
Let's take them down before they get wet.

371
22:01.033 --> 22:02.660
Yes, sir.

372
22:03.701 --> 22:06.781
This laundry's all tangled up.

373
22:06.781 --> 22:11.881
It'll come off if you do it slowly. Be patient and take your time.

374
22:11.881 --> 22:13.633
Yes, sir!

375
22:15.085 --> 22:16.530
Corporal Park Min Seok.

376
22:16.530 --> 22:18.831
Se Gye, what's up?

377
22:19.501 --> 22:21.924
Corporal Im Da Hye is looking for Bit Na Ri.

378
22:21.924 --> 22:25.072
Bit Na Ri? If Corporal Im Da Hye calls, you should go.

379
22:25.072 --> 22:27.201
I'll do this, so you go.

380
22:27.201 --> 22:28.849
No, sir. I should help you with this.

381
22:28.849 --> 22:30.284
It's okay. Go on.

382
22:32.601 --> 22:34.720
Good luck, Se Gye.

383
22:50.061 --> 22:53.761
Hyeon Uk, I'll do this side.

384
22:53.761 --> 22:55.417
Yes, sir.

385
23:05.134 --> 23:08.741
Darn it. The laundry will all get wet.

386
23:08.741 --> 23:11.986
I can't just take them from other units...

387
23:12.901 --> 23:14.561
Corporal Park Min Seok?

388
23:14.561 --> 23:17.806
It's raining. Please come over here.

389
23:26.334 --> 23:27.830
Thanks.

390
23:36.679 --> 23:40.621
Even things that seem impossible to untangle will eventually come undone if you try.

391
23:40.621 --> 23:42.281
You're right.

392
23:42.281 --> 23:47.551
Even if it's this tangled, if you take it slow, it'll all...

393
23:51.031 --> 23:52.864
Oh, Hyeon Uk.

394
23:52.864 --> 23:56.561
Actually, I heard from the Company Commander.

395
23:56.561 --> 23:59.341
What? Oh, really?

396
23:59.341 --> 24:04.191
He said he'd keep it a secret... Oh, Company Commander.

397
24:05.737 --> 24:09.683
To be honest, this past year was very hard.

398
24:10.333 --> 24:12.229
It felt like lost time.

399
24:13.541 --> 24:16.415
My college friends who enlisted with me were going on leave,

400
24:16.415 --> 24:20.533
while I was just wasting time in hospitals for rehab and everything...

401
24:22.457 --> 24:26.407
Honestly, I resented you, Corporal Park.

402
24:27.403 --> 24:29.678
But whether it was fate or ill fate,

403
24:29.678 --> 24:34.716
when we met again here, I remembered all that lost time.

404
24:34.716 --> 24:38.931
My resentment grew, and I wanted to get revenge.

405
24:40.377 --> 24:42.477
But...

406
24:42.477 --> 24:46.927
eating, sleeping, and spending time in the same barracks,

407
24:47.700 --> 24:51.897
I gradually realized that I was wrong.

408
24:51.897 --> 24:55.482
The division commander's son, Park Min Seok,

409
24:55.482 --> 24:57.337
whom I always resented,

410
24:57.337 --> 25:02.169
was just a version I created because I was bitter about my situation.

411
25:02.169 --> 25:07.570
I didn't realize how hard you worked to endure everything more than anyone else.

412
25:09.217 --> 25:11.927
It's all my fault

413
25:12.809 --> 25:14.191
that things have come to this point.

414
25:14.191 --> 25:19.677
No, it's all my fault.

415
25:19.677 --> 25:23.657
Either way, you misunderstood because of me,

416
25:23.657 --> 25:26.840
and you went to the hospital late because of me.

417
25:27.577 --> 25:30.379
Without knowing your situation

418
25:30.379 --> 25:32.937
or what you went through,

419
25:32.937 --> 25:36.371
I was just happy to see you again.

420
25:39.983 --> 25:41.780
- I'm s-- - I'm s--

421
25:42.797 --> 25:44.607
- I'm sorr-- - I'm sorr--

422
25:44.607 --> 25:46.989
- You first... - You go first.

423
25:54.423 --> 25:56.088
Corporal Park Min Seok.

424
25:56.762 --> 25:58.237
Yeah?

425
25:58.237 --> 26:02.139
I'm really... I'm really sorry.

426
26:02.895 --> 26:04.467
No...

427
26:05.729 --> 26:08.413
I'm really... I'm really sorry...

428
26:08.413 --> 26:10.802
No, sir. I'm more sorry...

429
26:12.857 --> 26:14.975
I'll do better from now on.

430
26:18.257 --> 26:20.197
Hyeon Uk.

431
26:20.197 --> 26:22.777
Let's take only the good memories

432
26:22.777 --> 26:26.697
from the training center and forget the bad.

433
26:26.697 --> 26:29.492
Instead, let's make

434
26:29.492 --> 26:33.016
a lot of great memories here to fill that void.

435
26:33.016 --> 26:35.971
I'll do my best as your senior!

436
26:37.417 --> 26:40.777
Shall we go grab some ramen?

437
26:40.777 --> 26:43.685
- I'd love to! - Alright, let's go!

438
26:43.685 --> 26:44.737
I'll carry that for you.

439
26:44.737 --> 26:49.497
- Jin, Shin, or Yuk? Which one? - I'll go with Jja, sir!

440
26:49.497 --> 26:51.554
- Jja? Good choice. - It's really pouring out there, sir!

441
26:51.554 --> 26:53.937
Hurry up. I'm going to have both Yuk and Shin.

442
26:53.937 --> 26:56.077
Didn't you say you were on a diet?

443
26:56.077 --> 26:58.821
Shin Ramyun is just a small cup.

444
27:00.557 --> 27:03.877
- Man, this is good, right? - It's delicious, sir.

445
27:03.877 --> 27:08.897
To be honest, I have had no appetite lately because of you.

446
27:08.897 --> 27:11.977
But didn't you eat Schnell Chicken last night, sir?

447
27:11.977 --> 27:14.762
Well, yeah, I'll always eat Schnell.

448
27:15.817 --> 27:18.057
But ramen... it's been a while.

449
27:18.057 --> 27:21.308
- Is your leg fully healed now? - Yes, I can even play soccer now.

450
27:21.308 --> 27:24.297
Min Seok has really matured.

451
27:24.297 --> 27:26.252
He certainly has.

452
27:28.357 --> 27:32.217
Since I told him that Hyeon Uk wasn't the one who posted on the cafe,

453
27:32.217 --> 27:34.677
I think Min Seok will be fine now.

454
27:34.677 --> 27:36.197
You did a great job, First Sergeant.

455
27:36.197 --> 27:38.900
Oh, it was nothing.

456
27:38.900 --> 27:42.007
You're the one who's going to have a hard time now.

457
27:43.617 --> 27:45.977
- You should get going, right? - Yes, sir.

458
27:45.977 --> 27:50.002
Have a good time. Don't mess up drinking.

459
27:50.002 --> 27:52.589
I mess up even when I'm sober.

460
27:53.298 --> 27:56.341
- That's true. - Don't worry, sir. Trust me!

461
27:56.341 --> 27:59.254
Alright, I trust you. Have fun.

462
27:59.254 --> 28:01.317
Call me if you need a second round.

463
28:01.317 --> 28:04.717
Oh, will do. I'll be off then.

464
28:04.717 --> 28:06.977
- Take care. - Yes, sir.

465
28:06.977 --> 28:08.277
- First Sergeant. - Yes?

466
28:08.277 --> 28:10.023
Thank you once again.

467
28:10.023 --> 28:12.723
- Oh, please. Just go have fun. - Yes, sir.

468
28:20.700 --> 28:22.427
Chungseong! I'm sorry I'm late.

469
28:22.427 --> 28:24.197
No, it's fine. I just got here early.

470
28:24.197 --> 28:26.499
- Please, have a seat. - Yes, sir.

471
28:27.177 --> 28:28.917
I'll grill the meat.

472
28:28.917 --> 28:30.741
I actually enjoy grilling.

473
28:30.741 --> 28:32.276
Yes, sir.

474
28:37.177 --> 28:39.197
This is uncomfortable, isn't it?

475
28:39.197 --> 28:42.117
Yes, to be honest, it's a bit awkward.

476
28:42.117 --> 28:45.577
Since it's awkward anyway, let's just say it's because I'm grilling.

477
28:45.577 --> 28:48.904
- It's not that, sir. - Are you not uncomfortable?

478
28:49.645 --> 28:51.440
I'm a little uncomfortable.

479
28:51.440 --> 28:52.850
I see...

480
28:54.237 --> 28:56.657
- Do you like soju? - Yes, I do.

481
28:56.657 --> 28:58.827
- Let's have a drink. - Yes, sir.

482
29:13.210 --> 29:18.381
Even though I know soju is bitter,

483
29:18.381 --> 29:20.571
I just keep drinking it.

484
29:23.717 --> 29:26.517
What kind of alcohol do you like?

485
29:26.517 --> 29:29.197
I like soju the best, sir.

486
29:29.197 --> 29:34.267
I think it's because the bitterness resembles my military life.

487
29:35.377 --> 29:39.696
Battalion Commander, you're like whiskey.

488
29:39.696 --> 29:44.727
- Whiskey? - Like an expensive 30-year-old one...

489
29:44.727 --> 29:50.417
Like whiskey on the rocks with high-quality ice in it.

490
29:50.417 --> 29:55.157
I think I'm more like the ice inside.

491
29:55.157 --> 29:57.259
- The ice, sir? - Yes.

492
29:57.879 --> 30:01.597
You never know when this ice will melt.

493
30:01.597 --> 30:05.931
It keeps that strong whiskey cool,

494
30:05.931 --> 30:10.684
but it doesn't really lower the proof.

495
30:10.684 --> 30:14.617
And while it might slow down how fast you get drunk,

496
30:14.617 --> 30:17.905
it can't stop the intoxication itself.

497
30:18.571 --> 30:24.092
That's exactly like my military life.

498
30:26.118 --> 30:27.805
I see.

499
30:30.753 --> 30:34.041
I'm talking nonsense.

500
30:34.041 --> 30:38.103
I'm not usually the type to open up,

501
30:38.103 --> 30:39.969
but I must feel comfortable with you.

502
30:39.969 --> 30:42.509
Thank you for saying that.

503
30:42.509 --> 30:45.897
No, I didn't mean it that way.

504
30:48.849 --> 30:52.939
I just... find myself acting that way.

505
30:53.894 --> 30:59.483
Yes. I also... want to be like you,

506
30:59.483 --> 31:02.629
someone like soju.

507
31:02.629 --> 31:07.649
Even if you swear you never want to see it again because of a killer hangover,

508
31:07.649 --> 31:12.489
you find yourself thinking of it come evening. Something like that?

509
31:12.489 --> 31:16.693
Exactly. That's the charm of soju.

510
31:19.588 --> 31:22.029
- Excuse me, sir. - No.

511
31:22.029 --> 31:23.689
I'll stop here.

512
31:23.689 --> 31:27.509
- Are you finished, sir? - At least one of us should stay sharp.

513
31:27.509 --> 31:29.449
That's also part of my position.

514
31:29.449 --> 31:32.538
As expected of the battalion commander.

515
31:35.229 --> 31:37.307
And...

516
31:38.355 --> 31:42.709
- about Defense Daily... - Oh! It's fine, Battalion Commander.

517
31:42.709 --> 31:47.749
I was a bit taken aback this morning, but I felt better soon after.

518
31:47.749 --> 31:50.060
Maybe it's because I have no regrets.

519
31:52.539 --> 31:54.168
Is that so?

520
31:54.989 --> 31:56.673
That's a relief.

521
31:59.849 --> 32:02.229
- Company Commander! - Yes?

522
32:02.229 --> 32:05.189
Only good things lie ahead for you.

523
32:05.189 --> 32:06.759
For me?

524
32:07.884 --> 32:10.809
I really hope so.

525
32:10.809 --> 32:14.401
I wish you nothing but the best as well, Battalion Commander.

526
32:14.401 --> 32:16.295
Thank you.

527
32:18.627 --> 32:20.900
Shall we have just one more?

528
32:20.900 --> 32:23.704
Oh! I'd love that!

529
32:24.609 --> 32:28.198
A bottle of soju and some ice, please.

530
32:29.849 --> 32:33.897
I used to drink it like this often.

531
32:33.897 --> 32:36.374
Give it a try.

532
32:41.001 --> 32:43.587
- Here. - Thank you.

533
32:51.386 --> 32:53.557
Not bad. How is it?

534
32:54.433 --> 32:59.897
It's cold and smooth. It goes down very easily.

535
32:59.897 --> 33:01.565
- Right? - Yes.

536
33:01.565 --> 33:05.649
I think it would be even better with a bit of lemon.

537
33:05.649 --> 33:09.863
You're right. Lemon would be good.

538
33:11.009 --> 33:14.589
I hope the First Sergeant can join us next time.

539
33:14.589 --> 33:16.512
Then... is the First Sergeant the lemon?

540
33:16.512 --> 33:20.562
Oh? I guess so.

541
33:21.919 --> 33:24.586
Let's have a drink with the First Sergeant like this often.

542
33:24.586 --> 33:26.340
That sounds great.

543
33:26.340 --> 33:28.018
Thank you.

544
33:37.769 --> 33:41.018
Ugh... I'm still not sober. This is bad.

545
33:41.709 --> 33:45.379
If I drink while hungover, I'm a total dog.

546
33:46.733 --> 33:48.029
- Company Commander! - First Sergeant?

547
33:48.029 --> 33:51.169
- It's... Chan Seok. - What about Chan Seok?

548
33:51.169 --> 33:54.908
- Just hurry! I'll explain on the way. - Why?

549
33:54.908 --> 33:56.578
- Just come quickly! - But I'm still drunk...

550
33:56.578 --> 33:58.684
I said hurry up!

551
34:03.329 --> 34:05.249
I'm sorry.

552
34:05.249 --> 34:06.630
Company Commander!

553
34:06.630 --> 34:08.512
Chan Seok!

554
34:10.259 --> 34:12.035
Byeong Nam!

555
34:19.154 --> 34:21.658
[12 hours ago] Hurry up and write.

556
34:21.658 --> 34:23.462
Hey, just do it roughly.

557
34:26.819 --> 34:29.070
- Have a good time. - Yes, sir!

558
34:29.070 --> 34:32.229
- Bring me a melon bar when you return. - Yes, sir!

559
34:32.229 --> 34:34.489
Platoon, attention!

560
34:34.489 --> 34:39.064
- Salute Sergeant First Class Im Seong Min! - Chungseong! Love you!

561
34:40.949 --> 34:45.479
At ease! Move out to the front gate!

562
34:46.253 --> 34:48.629
Keep your wits about you and don't drink too much.

563
34:48.629 --> 34:52.609
If Se Gye's face is recognized, people will swarm, so let's avoid crowds.

564
34:52.609 --> 34:55.729
- I'll stick to him like a manager. - I'll be his bodyguard.

565
34:55.729 --> 34:58.319
A night out with a star is tough.

566
34:58.319 --> 35:01.129
Thank you, everyone.

567
35:01.129 --> 35:06.194
But everyone will recognize me because of my unmistakable gaze.

568
35:06.792 --> 35:07.801
Here he goes again.

569
35:07.801 --> 35:11.649
- I'm sorry for making you suffer. - Hey, cover this punk's eyes.

570
35:11.649 --> 35:13.989
- Shouldn't we cover his mouth first? - You forgot your meds, didn't you?

571
35:13.989 --> 35:15.378
Private Jeon Se Gye! I want to see.

572
35:15.378 --> 35:16.594
- Whoa! - What is it?

573
35:16.594 --> 35:18.309
Oh! It's almost time for the bus!

574
35:18.309 --> 35:21.319
Hey, hey! Run, run!

575
35:24.169 --> 35:26.279
- Oh, man. - Hey!

576
35:27.876 --> 35:31.111
Hey, right, right! Left, left!

577
35:35.909 --> 35:38.009
Something's weird.

578
35:38.009 --> 35:42.029
Is this a prank? No one recognizes Jeon Se Gye.

579
35:42.029 --> 35:45.429
He's the nation's actor, Jeon Se Gye!

580
35:45.429 --> 35:47.215
- Se Gye. - Private Jeon Se Gye.

581
35:47.215 --> 35:48.815
Don't be discouraged.

582
35:48.815 --> 35:50.774
It's okay.

583
35:50.774 --> 35:55.609
I've gained weight since enlisting, so they don't notice.

584
35:55.609 --> 36:00.729
Even if they do, my aura will...

585
36:03.828 --> 36:07.237
Let's go for a drink before Se Gye's ego gets crushed.

586
36:10.549 --> 36:12.249
- Se Gye. - Private Jeon Se Gye.

587
36:12.249 --> 36:14.449
- Are you okay? - Sergeant Kang Chan Seok.

588
36:14.449 --> 36:16.249
Would you like a cigarette?

589
36:17.008 --> 36:19.357
- Yeah, let's go smoke first. - Sounds good!

590
36:19.357 --> 36:22.749
- I'll just relax and have fun! - Let's go!

591
36:22.749 --> 36:24.129
Shoot, shoot!

592
36:24.129 --> 36:26.549
Corporal Kim Dong Woo, isn't she pretty?

593
36:26.549 --> 36:29.979
I'm seeing her on leave. Want to time it together?

594
36:29.979 --> 36:31.429
[2013 College Entrance Exam] I'll cover the rear.

595
36:31.429 --> 36:33.809
- I'll take the three-way. - I'll take the short.

596
36:33.809 --> 36:36.789
Man, I'm paying my own money to shoot guns even when I'm out.

597
36:36.789 --> 36:39.637
- Isn't this a soldier's fate? - You're right.

598
36:39.637 --> 36:41.479
[PC Cafe: 3,000 won per hour] [Garrison Area Special Rate]

599
36:41.479 --> 36:43.017
Did you see that headshot?

600
36:47.289 --> 36:49.489
- Here. - Corporal Cha Byeong Ho.

601
36:49.489 --> 36:51.238
- I'm not getting drunk. - I wish you a long life, sir.

602
36:51.238 --> 36:53.395
[Regular Menu vs. Military Menu] (Military Menu is more expensive)

603
36:53.395 --> 36:56.798
- Ma'am, can we get a refill on the soup? - Yeah.

604
36:56.798 --> 36:59.435
- Hey, just order a new one. - Are you buying?

605
36:59.435 --> 37:02.233
- Se Gye, is that okay? - Drink as much as you want today.

606
37:02.233 --> 37:04.149
Then one more special order, please.

607
37:04.149 --> 37:05.940
- Should we get boiled pork? - Boiled pork!

608
37:05.940 --> 37:08.331
Two large orders of boiled pork, please.

609
37:08.331 --> 37:11.849
To our squad's overnight stay! Cheers!

610
37:19.028 --> 37:21.088
[Paradise of Life]

611
37:24.870 --> 37:27.349
Hey, I'm paying, so don't order too much, okay?

612
37:27.349 --> 37:29.091
If the wrap vegetables are free, can't we eat more?

613
37:29.091 --> 37:30.042
Yeah, order more!

614
37:30.042 --> 37:33.189
[Military Table Fee: 10,000 won per person] Sir, more wrap vegetables, please.

615
37:33.189 --> 37:37.706
♪ To find the person I've always dreamed of ♪

616
37:38.529 --> 37:42.237
♪ I'll go on a trip for myself ♪

617
37:45.794 --> 37:48.600
[1 Hour: Regular 15,000 / Military 35,000] ♪ Even when the rough wind blows ♪

618
37:48.600 --> 37:51.909
So, I saw this really beautiful woman.

619
37:51.909 --> 37:54.069
- Should I set you up? - Is she pretty?

620
37:54.069 --> 37:56.469
- Are you okay with older women? - How old?

621
37:56.469 --> 37:58.323
35.

622
37:59.106 --> 38:00.612
Byeong Ho says he doesn't have a girlfriend.

623
38:00.612 --> 38:02.809
[Extra charge for soldiers] [Unlimited pickled radish refills]

624
38:02.809 --> 38:05.859
♫ Give me your love ♫

625
38:05.859 --> 38:08.118
Like that!

626
38:12.928 --> 38:14.424
Oh, my throat.

627
38:14.424 --> 38:16.547
Whoa! Cha Byeong Ho! Cha Byeong Ho!

628
38:16.547 --> 38:19.292
- Cha Byeong Ho! - Cha Byeong Ho!

629
38:19.292 --> 38:21.265
[Military Price, Additional charge 3,000 won per chicken]

630
38:27.629 --> 38:30.029
This is what I'm most afraid of.

631
38:30.029 --> 38:32.629
I look so cute.

632
38:32.629 --> 38:38.109
You said you didn't like taking photos, but you look like you're having the most fun.

633
38:38.109 --> 38:40.560
- I didn't know I'd be this cute. - You are cute.

634
38:40.560 --> 38:42.588
Wow, it's 8:00 PM already. I'm starting to get tired.

635
38:42.588 --> 38:44.689
You can't sleep tonight. Every second is precious!

636
38:44.689 --> 38:46.519
That's right!

637
38:48.509 --> 38:52.029
Hey, mister! Watch where you're going!

638
38:52.029 --> 38:56.739
- I'm sorry. - Ugh, that soldier smell is disgusting.

639
38:56.739 --> 38:59.808
Let's go. What a total loser, seriously.

640
39:01.297 --> 39:03.687
Don't those kids have uncles at home?

641
39:03.687 --> 39:06.719
Talking about smell to a soldier protecting the country?

642
39:06.719 --> 39:07.973
What's wrong? Are you drunk?

643
39:07.973 --> 39:10.749
- Let's go. - Yes, sir.

644
39:10.749 --> 39:12.663
For another drink?

645
39:17.647 --> 39:19.206
Hey, give me a cigarette.

646
39:19.857 --> 39:22.708
Damn, 200,000 won? Are you kidding me?

647
39:22.708 --> 39:24.329
Is this a hotel or something?

648
39:24.329 --> 39:27.869
They shouldn't rip us off like this. It's even more expensive than last time.

649
39:27.869 --> 39:30.949
This is way too much. It's more than our monthly salary.

650
39:30.949 --> 39:33.109
Let's look elsewhere. There must be a place.

651
39:33.109 --> 39:36.069
But what if it's the same everywhere else?

652
39:36.069 --> 39:38.185
There will be. Let's go.

653
39:39.869 --> 39:42.300
Or maybe today...

654
39:42.964 --> 39:45.569
- Oppa! It's them! - Right.

655
39:45.569 --> 39:48.329
What? Oh, they're just soldiers?

656
39:48.329 --> 39:52.049
Those guys checked us out, then laughed at us.

657
39:52.049 --> 39:55.268
Checking you out? Hey, you guys are students, aren't you?

658
39:55.268 --> 39:57.395
Cha Byeong Ho, stay out of this.

659
39:57.395 --> 40:00.494
Oh, "stay out of this."

660
40:00.494 --> 40:02.649
Group, attention!

661
40:06.907 --> 40:08.455
At ease!

662
40:09.952 --> 40:12.840
- What the... - Hey there, Mr. Soldier.

663
40:12.840 --> 40:16.791
You should focus on your duty to the nation, not your animal instincts.

664
40:17.624 --> 40:21.006
Look, I think there's a misunderstanding.

665
40:21.006 --> 40:22.754
We weren't checking you out.

666
40:22.754 --> 40:24.023
What are you talking about?

667
40:24.023 --> 40:26.799
Anyway, I'm sorry if we offended you.

668
40:26.799 --> 40:30.889
Hey, are you saying my girls are lying right now?

669
40:32.213 --> 40:34.349
Forget it! Hey, take a picture!

670
40:34.349 --> 40:37.136
Just take a picture of them. Post it on Facebook!

671
40:37.136 --> 40:39.059
- School them! - Do it!

672
40:41.053 --> 40:45.612
If we made you uncomfortable, I sincerely apologize. I'm sorry.

673
40:45.612 --> 40:48.615
Put the phone down. "I'm sorry, brother?"

674
40:48.615 --> 40:53.120
Then let's go talk for a second. Huh? Let's go.

675
40:53.120 --> 40:56.425
Let's go over there and we'll explain.

676
40:56.425 --> 40:59.099
Fuck. The world's gone to hell.

677
41:01.429 --> 41:05.629
Brother, then just give us 200,000 won as a settlement.

678
41:05.629 --> 41:09.489
- You little... - Then we won't call the police and let it go.

679
41:09.489 --> 41:12.723
- Hey, that's cheap. - Is it really that cheap?

680
41:12.723 --> 41:15.201
- It's damn cheap. - What?

681
41:24.067 --> 41:25.663
Wait a second.

682
41:27.571 --> 41:29.152
- What? - Where are you going?

683
41:29.152 --> 41:31.041
- He's chicken. - Totally chicken.

684
41:31.041 --> 41:34.709
I'll handle things here, so take Se Gye and head inside.

685
41:34.709 --> 41:37.458
- Sergeant Kang Chan Seok. - Don't worry, just go.

686
41:38.209 --> 41:40.742
I said go. Se Gye is with you.

687
41:45.655 --> 41:47.338
Just go inside.

688
41:47.338 --> 41:50.153
Sergeant Kang Chan Seok. You're being discharged soon.

689
41:50.153 --> 41:53.249
- I know. Go. Don't worry. - Let's go.

690
41:53.931 --> 41:55.722
Hey, they're leaving.

691
41:55.722 --> 41:58.143
Hey, soldiers!

692
41:58.143 --> 42:00.129
What's up with Korean soldiers?

693
42:00.129 --> 42:03.758
I'm so scared, I might die.

694
42:05.067 --> 42:08.359
- Hey. He's coming, he's coming. - Oh.

695
42:10.709 --> 42:12.229
Why aren't you leaving?

696
42:12.229 --> 42:15.202
I'm worried about the kids, not you.

697
42:15.202 --> 42:17.332
You might lose your cool.

698
42:18.889 --> 42:20.889
Guys, I'm really sorry.

699
42:21.535 --> 42:25.019
I don't have much money on me right now, but...

700
42:27.189 --> 42:29.479
Let's just settle this with this.

701
42:29.479 --> 42:32.592
What? 50,000 won? Is that all you got, mister? Huh?

702
42:32.592 --> 42:33.949
Give us 2,000 won more.

703
42:33.949 --> 42:37.069
What are you doing? Why give them money when we did nothing wrong?

704
42:37.069 --> 42:40.289
- Leave if you're going to interfere. - Get out of my way, damn it...

705
42:40.289 --> 42:44.813
You soldiers go to the stockade if you fight with us, right?

706
42:44.813 --> 42:48.613
Right? Then give us 100,000 won more.

707
42:48.613 --> 42:50.353
Then we'll really leave you alone.

708
42:50.353 --> 42:53.833
I really don't have any more money. So please, just take this.

709
42:53.833 --> 42:57.373
Liar! Let's check his pockets, guys.

710
42:57.373 --> 43:01.793
- Wait, guys. Stop it. - Where is it? Grab it! Is this his wallet?

711
43:01.793 --> 43:03.458
- Guys, stop it. - Look at this.

712
43:03.458 --> 43:05.917
Take it out. What's this?

713
43:05.917 --> 43:08.184
What? This is crazy!

714
43:09.212 --> 43:11.153
Hey, what is this?

715
43:11.153 --> 43:14.467
The soldiers took a group photo! How cute!

716
43:14.467 --> 43:17.202
Where is it? Oh, here it is!

717
43:17.202 --> 43:19.033
Hey, mister.

718
43:19.033 --> 43:21.733
How's this? Huh?

719
43:21.733 --> 43:25.366
See? You should've just given us the money. Right? Am I right?

720
43:30.944 --> 43:33.822
- Got hurt? - You saw that, right? You all saw it!

721
43:33.822 --> 43:35.196
You saw the soldier hit a civilian, right?

722
43:35.196 --> 43:37.523
It hurts! Record this! Ow!

723
43:37.523 --> 43:39.923
Hey! The soldier definitely hit...

724
43:41.273 --> 43:42.976
What? You gonna hit me?

725
43:42.976 --> 43:45.713
Why have you been acting so tough this whole time?

726
43:45.713 --> 43:47.913
Just die then!

727
43:47.913 --> 43:51.135
Whoa, he's tough.

728
43:51.135 --> 43:53.253
Hey, hit him!

729
43:53.926 --> 43:56.586
Watch this. Hey!

730
44:01.124 --> 44:02.870
Chan Seok!

731
44:07.035 --> 44:11.431
- A soldier is hitting someone! - A soldier is hitting a civilian!

732
44:15.820 --> 44:21.144
- A soldier is hitting us! - A soldier is hitting someone!

733
44:30.363 --> 44:32.130
Chungseong!

734
44:32.130 --> 44:34.038
- Chungseong! - Chungseong!

735
44:35.053 --> 44:38.163
Kang Chan Seok! Sergeant Kang Chan Seok.

736
44:40.653 --> 44:42.353
Goodness.

737
44:44.253 --> 44:49.503
I'm sorry, Battalion Commander. I've caused unnecessary trouble.

738
44:55.873 --> 44:57.513
How are the men doing?

739
44:57.513 --> 45:00.793
Fortunately, no fractures. Just some bruises and abrasions.

740
45:00.793 --> 45:02.953
That's a relief.

741
45:02.953 --> 45:07.313
But sir, Chan Seok was actually quite admirable...

742
45:07.313 --> 45:09.453
He held back until the very end.

743
45:09.453 --> 45:12.813
He used to be a troublemaker and a notorious fighter back in Bupyeong.

744
45:12.813 --> 45:18.283
He just took the beating to protect his juniors, even while being humiliated.

745
45:19.053 --> 45:20.573
What about those punks?

746
45:20.573 --> 45:26.083
Well, the local police station ruled it as mutual assault.

747
45:27.521 --> 45:28.553
Mutual assault?

748
45:28.553 --> 45:32.566
They couldn't fight back as soldiers and were just getting beaten up.

749
45:32.566 --> 45:35.357
The police must have been mindful of the local merchants' complaints.

750
45:35.357 --> 45:39.043
They ruled it mutual assault based solely on the assailants' statements.

751
45:41.013 --> 45:44.473
Plus, since the assailants are minors, they were released with a warning.

752
45:44.473 --> 45:46.243
A warning?

753
45:47.686 --> 45:52.002
Even if they're minors, a soldier was beaten by punks and they're just let go?

754
45:52.002 --> 45:53.377
This is so embarrassing, damn it.

755
45:53.377 --> 45:57.963
What does this town think of us soldiers, from the kids to the police?

756
46:01.270 --> 46:03.102
[Regimental Commander]

757
46:06.833 --> 46:09.073
Chungseong! This is Battalion Commander Byeon Hyeok Jin, sir.

758
46:09.073 --> 46:13.333
Hey, is your unit cursed? There's never a quiet day with you guys.

759
46:13.333 --> 46:14.393
I am sorry, sir.

760
46:14.393 --> 46:18.633
Just keep this one quiet. Settle it and be done with it.

761
46:18.633 --> 46:23.673
Sir, our soldier was injured. How can we just let this go?

762
46:23.673 --> 46:24.853
Hey, Byeon Hyeok Jin.

763
46:24.853 --> 46:26.973
Don't you see the situation?

764
46:26.973 --> 46:30.513
With the firearm leak, you want noise about assaulting civilians too?

765
46:30.513 --> 46:33.133
It wasn't an assault on civilians.

766
46:33.133 --> 46:35.453
It was a one-sided lynching of a soldier.

767
46:35.453 --> 46:39.476
Listen! This area is where the corps and division are stationed.

768
46:39.476 --> 46:41.904
If the locals turn against us,

769
46:41.904 --> 46:43.813
even the Ministry of Defense will hear about it!

770
46:43.813 --> 46:46.469
Wrap it up by tomorrow and report back.

771
46:55.213 --> 46:59.193
Oh, Regimental Commander, sir. You didn't have to do that.

772
46:59.193 --> 47:05.193
Chairman Kim, this Byeon Hyeok Jin is so stubborn. It's quite exhausting.

773
47:05.193 --> 47:09.273
I've paved the way for you, so go and talk to him.

774
47:09.273 --> 47:12.443
Use this chance to get to know him.

775
47:12.443 --> 47:15.737
Those rigid types need a little greasing to get them moving.

776
47:15.737 --> 47:18.753
That'll surely soften him up, won't it?

777
47:18.753 --> 47:22.993
Anyway, the weather is great lately. You should come out for a game of golf!

778
47:22.993 --> 47:26.052
- Shall we play a round of golf? - I'll handle the booking, sir.

779
47:30.373 --> 47:33.303
What's going on?

780
47:34.753 --> 47:39.106
Hey, everyone, relax. It'll be okay.

781
47:39.106 --> 47:42.993
Right. With so many witnesses, they won't just let us be victimized.

782
47:42.993 --> 47:45.853
I'll testify to the military police and the Ministry of Defense.

783
47:45.853 --> 47:48.713
I'll post it on the e-People petition site as soon as duty ends.

784
47:48.713 --> 47:53.353
I'll even mobilize my fans to make sure we get a petition signed.

785
47:53.353 --> 47:56.593
Or I'll... talk to my dad properly this time!

786
47:56.593 --> 47:58.564
Those bastards!

787
47:59.173 --> 48:00.453
You crazy bastard.

788
48:00.453 --> 48:01.989
If your dad gets involved, you'll make

789
48:01.989 --> 48:05.673
the Battalion Commander and Company Commander look like fools.

790
48:05.673 --> 48:09.418
I know how you feel, but I'm sure they're figuring out what to do.

791
48:09.418 --> 48:11.393
Don't overstep and ruin things.

792
48:11.393 --> 48:13.443
Yes, sir.

793
48:19.438 --> 48:21.068
You're back?

794
48:32.373 --> 48:35.793
It's nothing, just a few scratches.

795
48:35.793 --> 48:39.067
But why are you all gathered here? It's embarrassing.

796
48:40.838 --> 48:46.715
Wow, Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam. Your jawline is no joke today.

797
48:46.715 --> 48:51.309
- Really? - The swelling made your jaw a perfect V-line.

798
48:51.309 --> 48:54.249
Why don't you just become a celebrity?

799
48:54.249 --> 48:57.629
Hey, Se Gye. Can't you hook him up with a celebrity audition or something?

800
48:57.629 --> 49:00.167
I think he could debut right away without even auditioning.

801
49:00.167 --> 49:01.939
Really?

802
49:01.939 --> 49:04.820
If I can't reach you once I'm discharged, you're dead.

803
49:04.820 --> 49:07.070
Don't worry, sir.

804
49:09.349 --> 49:11.395
Sergeant Kang Chan Seok?

805
49:11.395 --> 49:12.769
Are you okay?

806
49:12.769 --> 49:14.479
I'm fine.

807
49:16.309 --> 49:20.369
But having that bandage there makes you look much softer.

808
49:20.369 --> 49:22.689
- Right. - Thanks...

809
49:22.689 --> 49:24.390
Please wait a moment.

810
49:25.749 --> 49:27.131
It's because it's covered.

811
49:27.131 --> 49:32.469
You'll be lonely if you're the only one, so I'll put one on too.

812
49:32.469 --> 49:35.209
- Don't overdo it. - You crazy bastard.

813
49:35.209 --> 49:38.729
You just had to stay there and get beaten up for nothing.

814
49:38.729 --> 49:41.709
Chan Seok, how could I leave you alone?

815
49:41.709 --> 49:44.069
Think of it as ending there because of me.

816
49:44.069 --> 49:47.789
If I hadn't helped tank the damage, your head would've split open.

817
49:47.789 --> 49:50.502
Fine, you're the best.

818
49:51.088 --> 49:52.829
Now, disperse.

819
49:52.829 --> 49:55.502
With all of you gathered here, it reeks of soldiers.

820
49:55.502 --> 49:57.409
Ugh, man...

821
49:57.409 --> 50:01.049
Hey, Se Gye. Go to the mess hall and bring me four raw eggs.

822
50:01.049 --> 50:05.714
- Yes, sir. - No, it's fine. It's just my face.

823
50:05.714 --> 50:07.639
What are you doing? Disperse.

824
50:07.639 --> 50:10.132
Yes, sir. Let's go.

825
50:10.132 --> 50:12.029
Get some rest, then.

826
50:12.029 --> 50:13.289
See you later.

827
50:13.289 --> 50:15.009
- Good work. - Good work.

828
50:15.009 --> 50:16.562
Get lost.

829
50:18.969 --> 50:21.633
Are you really okay?

830
50:21.633 --> 50:22.758
Yeah.

831
50:22.758 --> 50:25.363
Man, I feel like I'm going to die.

832
50:25.363 --> 50:29.488
Geez... what's with the mood in this unit?

833
50:29.488 --> 50:31.156
I know, right?

834
50:32.149 --> 50:35.093
- Stand up straight, man. - Sorry.

835
50:40.788 --> 50:42.230
Chungseong!

836
50:42.915 --> 50:46.469
May I have your name and the purpose of your visit?

837
50:46.469 --> 50:48.343
Oh, you're working hard.

838
50:48.343 --> 50:52.800
I'm Kim Young Chul, the president of the Yooncheon-ri Merchants Association.

839
50:52.800 --> 50:55.177
I have an appointment with the Battalion Commander.

840
50:55.177 --> 50:56.553
Yes, sir. I'll open the gate right away!

841
50:56.553 --> 51:00.688
I own the barbecue place. I guess you haven't been there yet, huh?

842
51:00.688 --> 51:01.767
Come visit sometime.

843
51:01.767 --> 51:04.305
- Yes, sir. - Alright.

844
51:12.642 --> 51:14.215
Oh, my.

845
51:15.629 --> 51:18.509
Hello, it's a pleasure to meet you. I'm...

846
51:18.509 --> 51:22.839
Kim Young Chul, the president of the Yooncheon-ri Merchants Association.

847
51:23.609 --> 51:29.519
I was on very close, brotherly terms with the previous battalion commander.

848
51:30.169 --> 51:32.689
I'm Battalion Commander Byeon Hyeok Jin.

849
51:32.689 --> 51:36.756
Oh, Company Commander. During the last sports day, our association sent over...

850
51:36.756 --> 51:40.489
Did the boys enjoy the three large watermelons we sent over?

851
51:40.489 --> 51:41.947
Yes.

852
51:42.654 --> 51:45.892
Our local merchants make a living thanks to the soldiers,

853
51:45.892 --> 51:48.769
and the soldiers benefit from us.

854
51:48.769 --> 51:52.759
Aren't we all one family working together for a win-win?

855
51:55.069 --> 51:59.229
I'm sure you didn't come here to talk about that. What is your business?

856
51:59.229 --> 52:02.769
Well, it's nothing else but...

857
52:02.769 --> 52:07.800
Two days ago, there was a bit of a misunderstanding between the local kids

858
52:07.800 --> 52:11.689
and the soldiers here.

859
52:11.689 --> 52:12.809
A misunderstanding?

860
52:12.809 --> 52:15.074
There's no need to make a big deal out of it.

861
52:15.074 --> 52:17.563
Battalion commander, if you could be generous and show some leniency,

862
52:17.563 --> 52:21.433
I'll treat the whole unit to a whole-hog barbecue dinner.

863
52:21.433 --> 52:23.709
How does that sound?

864
52:23.709 --> 52:25.750
Whole-hog barbecue...

865
52:26.383 --> 52:28.069
Look here, Mr. President.

866
52:28.069 --> 52:32.569
My boys couldn't even defend themselves just because they were in uniform.

867
52:32.569 --> 52:35.029
They were trampled on by local high schoolers.

868
52:35.029 --> 52:38.909
It was just a little scuffle between kids. Why make such a fuss over a few scratches?

869
52:38.909 --> 52:41.649
The state provided those uniforms.

870
52:41.649 --> 52:44.041
They were mocked and beaten while wearing those uniforms,

871
52:44.041 --> 52:47.209
and you're calling that a "scuffle?"

872
52:47.209 --> 52:50.997
Do you think my men are just local suckers

873
52:50.997 --> 52:53.406
who will shut their mouths and be happy if you throw them a bit of meat?

874
52:53.406 --> 52:57.049
Is that how you see us?

875
52:57.049 --> 52:58.889
Now, Battalion Commander.

876
52:58.889 --> 53:02.749
You haven't been here long, so you don't seem to have a feel for things yet.

877
53:02.749 --> 53:07.689
As Captain Cho knows, once public opinion in this town turns against you,

878
53:07.689 --> 53:10.869
it's going to be quite difficult for you to run this unit.

879
53:10.869 --> 53:13.485
You should've disciplined your kids better.

880
53:13.485 --> 53:15.140
Sir, you're being...

881
53:22.169 --> 53:24.499
Mr. Kim Young Chul.

882
53:27.329 --> 53:30.749
Why don't you worry about disciplining your own kids?

883
53:30.749 --> 53:33.547
"Your own kids?"

884
53:34.715 --> 53:37.926
Is that how you're going to be, Lieutenant Colonel Byeon Hyeok Jin?

885
53:37.926 --> 53:41.675
If a young man like you is this rigid, things are going to get...

886
53:41.675 --> 53:46.061
well, very difficult for you.

887
53:46.689 --> 53:52.489
Fine. From now on, let's just each look out for ourselves.

888
53:52.489 --> 53:55.719
Don't come crying to me later.

889
53:57.169 --> 53:58.589
I came here to have a civil talk,

890
53:58.589 --> 54:01.272
but if you're going to be like this, it's going to be exhausting.

891
54:01.272 --> 54:05.179
Good grief. Damn it.

892
54:25.429 --> 54:27.184
- Yoon Mo. - Corporal Sung Yoon Mo.

893
54:27.184 --> 54:29.875
- Let's go! - Yes, sir.

894
54:31.899 --> 54:34.931
- Is it three pages? - Yes, that's right.

895
54:35.817 --> 54:38.353
It's coming along too slowly, though.

896
54:39.028 --> 54:44.249
Okay, here's a question.

897
54:44.249 --> 54:48.055
I'm going on overnight leave next week, so what should our Yoon Mo do?

898
54:48.055 --> 54:52.029
- Work my ass off. - Exactly! Here!

899
54:52.029 --> 54:54.689
Corporal Sung Yoon Mo... What is this?

900
54:54.689 --> 54:59.039
It's the "No Hee Jeong Handover Form" for everything you need to do while I'm gone.

901
54:59.758 --> 55:03.592
No Hee Jeong's Handover Form: 1. Close the monthly troop settlement early.

902
55:03.592 --> 55:07.051
2. Print reward vacation certificates. 3. Update warehouse equipment ledger.

903
55:07.051 --> 55:09.569
4. Organize daily duty roster... Replace status board acetate.

904
55:09.569 --> 55:10.989
Maintain method acting of looking busy.

905
55:10.989 --> 55:12.489
Follow First Sergeant's orders immediately.

906
55:12.489 --> 55:15.139
Replenish tea time supplies for officers.

907
55:16.329 --> 55:18.309
Do I really have to do all this?

908
55:18.309 --> 55:22.252
Then who will? Me? I'm on leave next week.

909
55:22.252 --> 55:24.152
Listen.

910
55:24.152 --> 55:26.503
Organize all the overdue unit logs,

911
55:26.503 --> 55:30.329
revise next week's training schedule, and submit it for approval.

912
55:30.329 --> 55:33.689
Just finish everything from 1 to 20 in order.

913
55:33.689 --> 55:38.130
If I have to work late on the day I return, you're a dead man.

914
55:39.609 --> 55:41.349
- Corporal No Hee Jeong. - Yeah?

915
55:41.349 --> 55:45.369
But couldn't you finish a few of these before you leave?

916
55:45.369 --> 55:47.344
There are still many weekdays left...

917
55:47.344 --> 55:49.584
This guy... I've had enough.

918
55:49.584 --> 55:51.289
Sung Yoon Mo.

919
55:51.289 --> 55:54.169
- Corporal Sung Yoon Mo! - As of now, your mouse is confiscated!

920
55:54.169 --> 55:55.989
- What? - It's confiscated!

921
55:55.989 --> 55:59.229
Corporal No Hee Jeong, really... You can't take the mouse.

922
55:59.229 --> 56:02.696
Doing paperwork without a mouse is so hard. Please give me a break.

923
56:02.696 --> 56:04.629
Haven't you memorized the shortcuts yet?

924
56:04.629 --> 56:07.149
- I've memorized them all. - What's Ctrl+N, T?

925
56:07.149 --> 56:09.869
- Copy cell! - Create table!

926
56:09.869 --> 56:12.189
I should just hit your Adam's apple...

927
56:12.189 --> 56:13.909
- Should I hit you with this or this? - No, wait.

928
56:13.909 --> 56:18.921
Announcement from the command center. All troops, assemble at the parade ground.

929
56:18.921 --> 56:20.769
Repeating the announcement.

930
56:20.769 --> 56:23.969
As of this moment, all battalion troops, assemble at the parade ground.

931
56:23.969 --> 56:25.945
Go check it out, you punk.

932
56:32.252 --> 56:34.436
Good luck, sir.

933
56:42.669 --> 56:45.717
Recently, our battalion members

934
56:45.717 --> 56:49.609
were assaulted by local high school students.

935
56:49.609 --> 56:53.568
But the merchant association conspired to

936
56:53.568 --> 56:57.729
cover it up as a mutual assault.

937
56:57.729 --> 57:02.169
Years of overcharging and unkindness were not enough,

938
57:02.169 --> 57:06.047
now they treat my boys, who devote their youth to protecting the country,

939
57:07.549 --> 57:10.909
worse than neighborhood dogs.

940
57:10.909 --> 57:13.169
I, the commander, will no longer stand by.

941
57:13.169 --> 57:14.889
Whoa. That's right.

942
57:14.889 --> 57:17.594
So, as of now,

943
57:17.594 --> 57:22.012
I am restricting all overnight and day leaves for this battalion.

944
57:22.829 --> 57:24.669
Restricting all leaves?

945
57:24.669 --> 57:26.449
I was supposed to go out tomorrow.

946
57:26.449 --> 57:28.799
I was scheduled to go this week.

947
57:30.169 --> 57:35.669
Instead! You can add these restricted leaves to your regular vacations.

948
57:35.669 --> 57:38.189
I will approve it all!

949
57:38.189 --> 57:41.461
Whether you use them for early discharge

950
57:41.461 --> 57:45.509
or add them to a regular vacation to go out for 15 days and get your fill,

951
57:45.509 --> 57:49.799
I'll let you use them at my discretion!

952
57:54.909 --> 57:57.350
Let's stick together

953
57:57.350 --> 58:01.668
and show them what happens when they disrespect soldiers.

954
58:14.036 --> 58:16.793
- Understood? - Yes, sir!

955
58:21.164 --> 58:24.038
Good. Thank you.

956
58:25.875 --> 58:27.575
Battalion, attention!

957
58:29.384 --> 58:31.303
Salute the Battalion Commander!

958
58:31.303 --> 58:34.127
- Chungseong! Love you! - Chungseong! Love you!

959
58:34.765 --> 58:37.215
Chungseong! Love you.

960
58:37.215 --> 58:39.668
Chungseong! Love you!

961
58:41.509 --> 58:44.730
As you were! Dismissed.

962
58:44.730 --> 58:46.425
Battalion Commander.

963
58:47.190 --> 58:50.129
I fully agree with the intent of restricting the troops.

964
58:50.129 --> 58:52.909
But there are many units that have Yooncheon-ri as their garrison area.

965
58:52.909 --> 58:57.809
I'm not sure if our battalion alone will impact the local economy...

966
58:57.809 --> 58:59.349
Operations Officer.

967
58:59.349 --> 59:03.739
When did I say only our battalion was doing this?

968
59:05.569 --> 59:07.878
Chungseong! Sir, it's Byeon Hyeok Jin.

969
59:07.878 --> 59:10.005
[One hour ago] I'm sorry to bother you. It's about something else.

970
59:10.005 --> 59:14.801
Two days ago, our boys were out and got beaten up by local high schoolers.

971
59:14.801 --> 59:17.069
What? Beaten up? Those punks...

972
59:17.069 --> 59:21.329
So starting this weekend, I'm restricting all leave and passes for my battalion.

973
59:21.329 --> 59:23.989
You're saying you need more backup?

974
59:23.989 --> 59:27.389
You're quick as always, sir. I'll take the lead on this.

975
59:27.389 --> 59:29.195
Please support us this time.

976
59:29.195 --> 59:31.489
Okay, deal. Let's wipe them out.

977
59:31.489 --> 59:32.829
Thank you, sir!

978
59:32.829 --> 59:35.809
Restricting the garrison area? I'm definitely in!

979
59:35.809 --> 59:38.509
I'll teach those people a lesson once and for all!

980
59:38.509 --> 59:41.389
I've canceled all officer dinners in Yooncheon-ri as of today!

981
59:41.389 --> 59:44.623
Letting them beat our boys is a matter of pride for the whole division.

982
59:44.623 --> 59:46.336
I'm ordering the restriction this weekend.

983
59:46.336 --> 59:49.018
Thank you! Chungseong!

984
59:51.529 --> 59:54.776
My place is always packed.

985
59:56.075 --> 59:58.129
Chungseong!

986
59:58.129 --> 01:00:00.089
Sergeant Major, what brings you here?

987
01:00:00.089 --> 01:00:01.929
[Return to your unit immediately!]

988
01:00:01.929 --> 01:00:03.369
I didn't quite catch that.

989
01:00:03.369 --> 01:00:05.369
[I said return to your units right now!]

990
01:00:05.369 --> 01:00:08.942
- Oh, I'll pour you a glass of soju. - Is that what he meant?

991
01:00:08.942 --> 01:00:12.196
[You frustrating punks!]

992
01:00:13.309 --> 01:00:15.670
Eat up, guys.

993
01:00:15.670 --> 01:00:16.679
[First Sergeant Park Jae Su]

994
01:00:16.679 --> 01:00:18.549
Chungseong! Sergeant Major! What's up?

995
01:00:18.549 --> 01:00:20.049
Yes!

996
01:00:22.635 --> 01:00:24.709
An interpreter? Yes, go ahead.

997
01:00:24.709 --> 01:00:27.355
You can interpret that? That's amazing.

998
01:00:28.208 --> 01:00:30.005
Everyone, attention!

999
01:00:33.469 --> 01:00:36.842
He says some punks beat up our men!

1000
01:00:39.181 --> 01:00:43.053
Everyone, return to base immediately! Move out!

1001
01:00:43.053 --> 01:00:44.929
- Move out! - Move out!

1002
01:00:44.929 --> 01:00:48.329
Hey, I'm sorry, but I have to go.

1003
01:00:48.329 --> 01:00:50.822
Hey, where are you going?

1004
01:00:52.486 --> 01:00:53.789
[All of you!]

1005
01:00:57.459 --> 01:00:58.609
Check, please!

1006
01:00:58.609 --> 01:01:00.392
Damn it.

1007
01:01:03.830 --> 01:01:06.037
Come back again soon!

1008
01:01:06.037 --> 01:01:08.953
Hey, did you calculate the soldiers' bill correctly?

1009
01:01:08.953 --> 01:01:11.299
Check it all. We'll bill them later.

1010
01:01:11.299 --> 01:01:13.117
Yes, I'll check it.

1011
01:01:13.785 --> 01:01:16.099
Geez... They're really playing hardball.

1012
01:01:16.099 --> 01:01:18.512
So what? What are they going to do?

1013
01:01:18.512 --> 01:01:21.409
- They won't last a few days, right? - Of course not, you punk!

1014
01:01:21.409 --> 01:01:26.149
Where else would they go in this town if not here?

1015
01:01:26.149 --> 01:01:27.594
Yes, well...

1016
01:01:28.379 --> 01:01:33.939
I'm going to teach them a proper lesson this time!

1017
01:01:33.939 --> 01:01:38.339
Wow. Battalion Commander really pressed the nuclear button.

1018
01:01:38.339 --> 01:01:39.823
I'm telling you.

1019
01:01:39.823 --> 01:01:45.679
If you look closely, you and the Battalion Commander are alike.

1020
01:01:45.679 --> 01:01:50.079
- We are? - You also have a short fuse.

1021
01:01:50.079 --> 01:01:53.329
The way you both explode is identical.

1022
01:01:54.798 --> 01:01:59.052
First Sergeant, you're my laugh button!

1023
01:01:59.052 --> 01:02:01.202
Pop, pop, pop!

1024
01:02:03.019 --> 01:02:04.959
- I think I just pressed it. - No, you didn't.

1025
01:02:04.959 --> 01:02:06.399
- I did. - No, you didn't.

1026
01:02:06.399 --> 01:02:08.325
- I did. - No.

1027
01:02:15.539 --> 01:02:20.739
If I hadn't gotten mixed up with those punks, I'd be on my final leave by now...

1028
01:02:20.739 --> 01:02:22.606
This is driving me crazy.

1029
01:02:23.952 --> 01:02:28.499
Hey, why are you pacing around like that? Does that make time go faster?

1030
01:02:28.499 --> 01:02:32.119
I should've been on my final leave... Damn.

1031
01:02:32.119 --> 01:02:34.199
Is it because you couldn't go out this time?

1032
01:02:34.199 --> 01:02:35.829
What?

1033
01:02:36.459 --> 01:02:37.959
I can't get ahold of Su Ah.

1034
01:02:37.959 --> 01:02:40.199
- Who's Su Ah? - My girlfriend.

1035
01:02:40.199 --> 01:02:44.499
- You didn't know that? - I'm not interested in other men's women.

1036
01:02:44.499 --> 01:02:49.909
It's 7:28 PM. Her class should be over, and she'd be waiting for the No. 77 bus...

1037
01:02:49.909 --> 01:02:54.088
Bus, my foot. At this hour, some cool older student...

1038
01:02:54.088 --> 01:02:57.469
would be picking her up in a foreign car.

1039
01:02:59.359 --> 01:03:02.919
- My Su Ah likes walking. - Who likes walking?

1040
01:03:02.919 --> 01:03:06.559
Besides, she's pure and innocent, like a white lily.

1041
01:03:06.559 --> 01:03:09.559
Not a lily, more like a mess tin.

1042
01:03:09.559 --> 01:03:11.875
- Lily, my ass. - But why can't you reach her?

1043
01:03:11.875 --> 01:03:14.165
- That's what I mean. - I don't know.

1044
01:03:14.165 --> 01:03:16.973
I don't know! I don't know!

1045
01:03:16.973 --> 01:03:19.329
Why are you getting so mad? Damn it...

1046
01:03:20.599 --> 01:03:22.499
I had such a good dream last night...

1047
01:03:22.499 --> 01:03:24.449
What did you dream about?

1048
01:03:25.079 --> 01:03:28.109
Su Ah came to see me on my discharge day...

1049
01:03:29.659 --> 01:03:33.159
- It's your birthday! - Take care, Sergeant!

1050
01:03:33.159 --> 01:03:36.098
Congratulations!

1051
01:03:38.239 --> 01:03:40.479
They were tossing me in the air like this.

1052
01:03:40.479 --> 01:03:43.810
You did it, honey! Congratulations!

1053
01:03:43.810 --> 01:03:48.419
She set up a whole buffet and came in a pretty car like this...

1054
01:03:48.419 --> 01:03:51.403
- and congratulated me. - Hey, dreams are usually the opposite.

1055
01:03:51.403 --> 01:03:54.259
Doesn't that mean you'll be single again?

1056
01:03:54.259 --> 01:03:57.499
Packages for Kang Min Gyu and Kwon Ki Woong.

1057
01:03:57.499 --> 01:04:00.496
What does this say? Ah, Byeong Nam.

1058
01:04:00.496 --> 01:04:03.149
Byeong Nam, to the admin office too.

1059
01:04:04.094 --> 01:04:07.444
What did I tell you? Dreams come true!

1060
01:04:10.739 --> 01:04:12.979
Jeon Se Gye! Bit Na Ri!

1061
01:04:12.979 --> 01:04:17.357
- Private Moon Bit Na Ri! Thank you! - Oh, Moon Bit Na Ri! Who's it from?

1062
01:04:17.357 --> 01:04:19.939
That's... a secret!

1063
01:04:19.939 --> 01:04:22.199
It's from his father.

1064
01:04:22.199 --> 01:04:24.039
No, it's not.

1065
01:04:24.039 --> 01:04:26.359
Chungseong. Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam. I'm here on business at the admin office.

1066
01:04:26.359 --> 01:04:29.179
- Oh, the Choi Soo Jong of Shinhwa Unit. - Sergeant Choi Soo Jong!

1067
01:04:29.179 --> 01:04:30.779
- Is Bang Su Ah your girlfriend? - Yes, sir!

1068
01:04:30.779 --> 01:04:32.139
Wow, this is huge.

1069
01:04:32.139 --> 01:04:34.759
It's not even close to the size of her love for me!

1070
01:04:34.759 --> 01:04:36.543
Cut the crap and open it. Move it!

1071
01:04:36.543 --> 01:04:38.339
Woof woof! Moving it!

1072
01:04:40.964 --> 01:04:43.979
Man... it really came.

1073
01:04:43.979 --> 01:04:45.677
I'm so jealous.

1074
01:04:45.677 --> 01:04:48.639
Oh? Couple shirts? I'm so jealous.

1075
01:04:48.639 --> 01:04:50.849
Wait, but the size...

1076
01:04:50.849 --> 01:04:53.321
Isn't it a bit small for you?

1077
01:04:54.186 --> 01:04:57.606
The sender is Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam...

1078
01:05:18.099 --> 01:05:20.638
A ring! Isn't this a proposal?

1079
01:05:20.638 --> 01:05:22.799
Corporal Park Min Seok. I think we need to head out for duty.

1080
01:05:22.799 --> 01:05:25.339
- No, there's still time left. - Go.

1081
01:05:25.339 --> 01:05:28.262
- Hurry up and go! Go! - Oh! Congratulations!

1082
01:05:28.262 --> 01:05:29.763
Seriously!

1083
01:05:29.763 --> 01:05:31.979
- Well... I'm heading out. - Yes. Let's go.

1084
01:05:31.979 --> 01:05:33.934
- Yes. - Yes.

1085
01:05:33.934 --> 01:05:35.344
Chungseong. Love you.

1086
01:05:35.344 --> 01:05:38.155
- Good work. - See you later.

1087
01:05:38.155 --> 01:05:40.983
Why is Su Ah's ring in here...

1088
01:05:40.983 --> 01:05:42.816
Didn't they break up?

1089
01:05:51.834 --> 01:05:53.755
Get out!

1090
01:05:57.078 --> 01:05:59.501
- Wait... no way! - Hey! Find Choi Byeong Nam!

1091
01:05:59.501 --> 01:06:00.959
Yes, sir.

1092
01:06:00.959 --> 01:06:06.029
For now, clear away anything hard or sharp around Byeong Nam.

1093
01:06:14.345 --> 01:06:16.935
Damn, why is there no balance?

1094
01:06:21.273 --> 01:06:23.339
This is a 1541 collect call.

1095
01:06:23.339 --> 01:06:26.359
While we connect, please state your name.

1096
01:06:26.359 --> 01:06:28.859
Su Ah, it's me, Byeong Nam. Please don't hang up and just pick up once!

1097
01:06:28.859 --> 01:06:32.789
The recipient does not wish to accept the call. Connection failed.

1098
01:06:35.537 --> 01:06:38.207
While we connect, please state your name.

1099
01:06:38.207 --> 01:06:40.751
Su Ah, what's wrong? I was wrong. Please let me hear your voice once!

1100
01:06:40.751 --> 01:06:42.779
The recipient does not wish to...

1101
01:06:45.559 --> 01:06:48.099
Su Ah, please...

1102
01:06:48.099 --> 01:06:50.526
Su Ah! Su Ah! It's me! Byeong Nam!

1103
01:06:51.428 --> 01:06:55.293
- Thanks for picking up. I really... - Huh? Who is this?

1104
01:06:57.013 --> 01:06:59.619
- Isn't this Su Ah's number? - No, it's not.

1105
01:06:59.619 --> 01:07:02.259
That can't be right. If Su Ah is next to you...

1106
01:07:02.259 --> 01:07:03.682
Could you put her on for a second?

1107
01:07:03.682 --> 01:07:08.309
You're thick-headed, aren't you? I said it's not Su Ah's number!

1108
01:07:09.547 --> 01:07:11.600
I'm not crying. Some dust got in my eye.

1109
01:07:11.600 --> 01:07:17.557
Why are so many guys looking for Su Ah today? It's costing me! Hang up now!

1110
01:07:22.487 --> 01:07:25.265
Oh, Su Ah! Did you eat?

1111
01:07:25.265 --> 01:07:27.792
I ate too. Yeah.

1112
